{
  "__doc__": "tools[] captured 2026-10-05 from real goose 1.53.0 requests (the x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu release binary, the CI guest's pin) against a local scripted /v1/messages stand-in, no Mandu in the path, with a throwaway GOOSE_PATH_ROOT, GOOSE_PROVIDER=anthropic and ANTHROPIC_HOST at the stand-in, in a network namespace with only loopback. name -> input_schema property names. \"1.53.0\" is the default surface of `goose run` and `goose session` (the developer, analyze, summon, skills, apps and extensionmanager platform extensions; scheduler and tom advertise no tool there). \"1.53.0 subagent\" is what a `delegate` subagent advertises (same provider, its own agent-session-id). \"1.53.0 --with-builtin <each>\" lists the tools each opt-in builtin or platform extension adds (code_execution, computercontroller, memory, chatrecall, todo, summarize, orchestrator, tutorial, autovisualiser; computercontroller's computer_control is macOS-only and absent here). \"1.53.0 +code_execution\" is the whole surface with code mode on: the non-developer tools move inside execute_typescript. \"1.53.0 --with-extension mandu-inspect:<cmd>\" is the U-LLM mount's spelling (`<name>__<tool>`, the name kept as given, hyphen included). Wire facts read in the same captures: POST /v1/messages only (no GET /v1/models at start for run or session), stream true, header agent-session-id (yyyymmdd_N), x-api-key; a tool_result's content is a plain string (shell: stderr then stdout, then \"Command exited with code N\" when non-zero). Pins arbiter/policy/goose-inbound.ts and tool-gate-surface.ts.",
